{
  "_comment": [
    "Pages yt-dlp can be pointed at, and what each one holds.",
    "",
    "One file, read by both sides: the extension loads it to decide when to offer",
    "a This page row, and the helper loads the same file to decide whether to ask",
    "for audio or video, whether to search when the direct pull fails, and whether",
    "to hand the job to yt-dlp at all. Two copies of this would drift apart within",
    "a week.",
    "",
    "Every entry below was checked against yt-dlp's own URL matching rather than",
    "assumed, using the sample URLs in test/test_host.py. A site is only listed as",
    "working where yt-dlp actually has an extractor that takes that shape of URL.",
    "",
    "ytdlp       false means we know the site and yt-dlp is not the answer there.",
    "            No This page row is offered and the helper will not route to it,",
    "            so whatever the network capture picks up is used instead. The",
    "            note says why. Absent means true.",
    "role        audio, video, or both. Drives whether yt-dlp is asked to",
    "            extract audio or to pick video plus audio and merge them.",
    "searchFallback  true where yt-dlp has no working extractor, checked against",
    "            its extractor list rather than assumed. The direct attempt still",
    "            runs first, and only when it fails is a matching recording",
    "            searched for, before any error is shown.",
    "endpoint    path segment on that host that holds media. Matched on segment",
    "            boundaries, and it may sit anywhere in the path, because these",
    "            sites put something variable in front: /{user}/status/{id}.",
    "match       a path pattern, for shapes a segment cannot express. Kept to the",
    "            syntax JavaScript and Python read the same way: classes, groups,",
    "            +*?, anchors and negative lookahead. No backreferences, no",
    "            lookbehind, no named groups.",
    "deny        first path segments on that host that never hold media. Checked",
    "            before anything else, because a bare two segment rule like",
    "            SoundCloud's cannot tell a track from /you/library."
  ],
  "version": 2,
  "sites": [
    {
      "hostname": "music.youtube.com",
      "label": "YouTube Music",
      "role": "audio",
      "searchFallback": false,
      "pages": [
        { "endpoint": "/watch", "role": "audio" },
        { "endpoint": "/playlist", "role": "audio" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "hostname": "youtu.be",
      "label": "YouTube",
      "role": "video",
